      "comment": "SOUTH SIDE STORY NZ (5) did some work from a wide barrier but stuck on and finished fourth last start, beaten 6.7 metres at Gloucester Park. Owns a good second-up record so should be improved and has won two of three attempts at this distance. Looks well placed. SUN PUBLISHER NZ (6) has been solid in two outings at Gloucester Park since coming from a similar barrier to this to win at Narrogin. Good enough to play a role. ALFA JESS (3) is in the mix having won in the city two back before coming from this draw for a respectable third at her most recent appearance here. ULTIMATE ZIPPER (9) is a consistent performer with three top-three finishes on the trot. Go well again.",
